00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:56.760
Why?

00:39:56.760 --> 00:39:58.600
For a few reasons.

00:39:58.600 --> 00:40:01.440
Business trends
including accessibility.

00:40:01.440 --> 00:40:03.840
So for us, accessibility
is very important.

00:40:03.840 --> 00:40:05.754
When we think about
how we provide access,

00:40:05.754 --> 00:40:07.170
whether through E
or prints, those

00:40:07.170 --> 00:40:10.410
are two key, of course, methods.

00:40:10.410 --> 00:40:13.110
But what we're seeing
with accessibility

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:20.370
is that the US census had about
9 million people identified

00:40:20.370 --> 00:40:25.850
in the United States alone that
were either hearing impaired

00:40:25.850 --> 00:40:27.140
or they were deaf.

00:40:27.140 --> 00:40:31.490
And it's a challenge
because only 39,000 Braille

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:33.440
books had been printed.

00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:35.780
It's a very small
percent of the population

00:40:35.780 --> 00:40:38.210
and not everybody has
access to Braille,

00:40:38.210 --> 00:40:41.365
nor do they all have
access to voice readers.

00:40:41.365 --> 00:40:43.490
What that means is the
percentage of the population

00:40:43.490 --> 00:40:45.860
that, potentially,
we can provide access

00:40:45.860 --> 00:40:47.420
to is significant.

00:40:47.420 --> 00:40:50.180
Not only when we think about
hearing impaired, but also

00:40:50.180 --> 00:40:52.070
learning impaired--
so people potentially

00:40:52.070 --> 00:40:54.830
with dyslexia who have a
hard time reading, kids who

00:40:54.830 --> 00:40:57.350
need that information
translated to them possibly,

00:40:57.350 --> 00:41:00.050
and also people for whom
English is a second language,

00:41:00.050 --> 00:41:02.000
and they want to be
able to quickly put

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:04.340
the audio and visual together.

00:41:04.340 --> 00:41:09.090
So we find that
accessibility is key for us.

00:41:09.090 --> 00:41:12.660
I'm going to give you a
