We do that today.

00:45:34.960 --> 00:45:37.460
Again, we do e-book
distribution.

00:45:37.460 --> 00:45:40.640
We bring that book content
into Ingram's CoreSource

00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:43.760
and then push it out to
the Google Cloud storage.

00:45:43.760 --> 00:45:47.360
The Cloud Functions-- so step
four includes three components.

00:45:47.360 --> 00:45:50.930
It includes translating
it to a wave file

00:45:50.930 --> 00:45:53.660
and then storing
it in Google Cloud.

00:45:53.660 --> 00:45:56.492
This is for all new
and changed content.

00:45:56.492 --> 00:45:57.950
If you think about
it, book content

00:45:57.950 --> 00:46:00.140
doesn't change that
much, unless it's new

00:46:00.140 --> 00:46:02.150
or unless new
editions come through.

00:46:02.150 --> 00:46:04.970
The Cloud Functions then pull
that new content or the change

00:46:04.970 --> 00:46:08.420
content through Cloud SQL
into two of our technologies,

00:46:08.420 --> 00:46:10.850
one, Aerio, which is
a tool that allows

00:46:10.850 --> 00:46:13.352
for written previews of books.

00:46:13.352 --> 00:46:14.810
Publishers house
it on their sites.

00:46:14.810 --> 00:46:17.240
And it allows them to
complete purchases.

00:46:17.240 --> 00:46:19.280
And the second is our
ipage application,

00:46:19.280 --> 00:46:21.985
which is it a
business-to-business solution.

00:46:24.780 --> 00:46:27.020
The second part of it is
also where the secret sauce

00:46:27.020 --> 00:46:27.710
happens, right?

00:46:27.710 --> 00:46:31.730
So the first part is
translating that text-to-speech

00:46:31.730 --> 00:46:33.720
and developing that wave file.

00:46:33.720 --> 00:46:36.860
The second part of it is
when a sample is collected--

00:46:36.860 --> 00:46:38.660
much like the sample
you just heard--

00:46:38.660 --> 00:46:42.950
we bring it into the
DialogFlow Enterprise Edition.

00:46:42.950 --> 00:46:47.270
And the system parses that
data, the title being the key,

00:46:47.270 --> 00:46:49.370
passes through
the Cloud DataFlow

00:46:49.370 --> 00:46:52.400
into Cloud SQL,
which then DialogFlow

00:46:52.400 --> 00:46:56.030
pulls that sample
out of the Cloud SQL,

00:46:56.030 --> 00:46:57.890
passes it through
the Cloud Functions.

00:46:57.890 --> 00:47:02.790
And then if transactions
are to exist,

00:47:02.790 --> 00:47:06.020
we pull it back into Google
Express for the conclusion

00:47:06.020 --> 00:47:07.230
of the transaction.

00:47:07.230 --> 00:47:09.410
So we can bring it all
the way through the sample

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:11.600
and listening to that
sample into the conclusion

00:47:11.600 --> 00:47:12.940
of a transaction.

00:47:12.940 --> 00:47:15.480
And we think that that's
going to be really powerful.

00:47:15.480 --> 00:47:19.460
So in conclusion-- I don't want
to get between you and dessert

00:47:19.460 --> 00:47:21.150
or what have you--

00:47:21.150 --> 00:47:23.780
we talked a little bit about
some of the business trends

00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:25.970
and what's happening
right now in the market.

00:47:25.970 --> 00:47:29.195
We talked a little bit about
the changes from physical to E

00:47:29.195 --> 00:47:30.410
to audio.

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:32.660
We talked about opportunities
around accessibility

00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:34.340
and closing the
loop between people

00:47:34.340 --> 00:47:39.350
who have needs and the systems
and the technology today

00:47:39.350 --> 00:47:42.350
and what we can do, what Google
has done with natural language.

00:47:42.350 --> 00:47:44.330
And we talked a little
bit about the technology

00:47:44.330 --> 00:47:45.920
and how we support it.

00:47:45.920 --> 00:47:47.760
I think we have
about 23 seconds.

00:47:47.760 --> 00:47:51.170
So I'll ask if there are any
questions either for any of us.

00:47:51.170 --> 00:47:52.370
[APPLAUSE]

00:47:52.370 --> 00:47:53.270
All right.

00:47:53.270 --> 00:47:54.770
Thank you.

00:47:54.770 --> 00:47:57.520
